:HELP NAME=ADDNETTBLE.Add Network Table Entry (ADDNETTBLE)
:P.Use the Add Network Table Entry (ADDNETTBLE) command to add a network
to the network table.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDNETTBLE/NETWORK'.Network (NETWORK)
:P.The network for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDNETTBLE/INTNETADR'.Internet address (INTNETADR)
:P.An internet address in dotted decimal form (IPv4) or in colon form
(IPv6).
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDNETTBLE/TEXT'.Text (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDNETTBLE/ALIASES'.Aliases (ALIASES)
:P.Other names the entry is known by.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ADDPCLTBLE.Add Protocol Table Entry (ADDPCLTBLE)
:P.Use the Add Protocol Table Entry (ADDPCLTBLE) command to add a
protocol to the protocol table.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPCLTBLE/PROTOCOL'.Protocol (PROTOCOL)
:P.The protocol for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPCLTBLE/PCLNBR'.Protocol number (PCLNBR)
:P.The protocol number for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPCLTBLE/TEXT'.Text (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDPCLTBLE/ALIASES'.Aliases (ALIASES)
:P.Other names the entry is known by.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ADDSRVTBLE.Add Service Table Entry (ADDSRVTBLE)
:P.Use the Add Service Table Entry (ADDSRVTBLE) command to add a service
to the services table.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDSRVTBLE/SERVICE'.Service (SERVICE)
:P.The service for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDSRVTBLE/PORT'.Port (PORT)
:P.The TCP or UDP port number.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDSRVTBLE/PROTOCOL'.Protocol (PROTOCOL)
:P.The protocol for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDSRVTBLE/TEXT'.Text (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDSRVTBLE/ALIASES'.Aliases (ALIASES)
:P.Other names the entry is known by.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ADDTCPHTE.Add TCP/IP Host Table Entry (ADDTCPHTE)
:P.Use the Add TCP/IP Host Table Entry (ADDTCPHTE) command to add an
address and its names to the host table.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPHTE/INTNETADR'.Internet address (INTNETADR)
:P.An internet address in dotted decimal form (IPv4) or in colon form
(IPv6).
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPHTE/HOSTNAME'.Host names (HOSTNAME)
:P.The host names for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 65 values can be given.
:P.The value has 1 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Name
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPHTE/TEXT'.Text (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ADDTCPIFC.Add TCP/IP Interface (ADDTCPIFC)
:P.Use the Add TCP/IP Interface (ADDTCPIFC) command to add an
interface&colon. an address on a line.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPIFC/INTNETADR'.Internet address (INTNETADR)
:P.An internet address in dotted decimal form (IPv4) or in colon form
(IPv6).
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*IP4DHCP:EPK.
:PD.The address is assigned by DHCP.
:PT.:PK.*IP6SAC:EPK.
:PD.The address is configured by IPv6 stateless autoconfiguration.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPIFC/LIND'.Line (LIND)
:P.The line description.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LOOPBACK, *VIRTUALIP, *OPC.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Line description
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. VLAN identifier
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 4094.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPIFC/SUBNETMASK'.Subnet mask (SUBNETMASK)
:P.The subnet mask that tells the network part of the address from the
host part.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*HOST:EPK.
:PD.A host route&colon. the address names a single host.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPIFC/TOS'.Type of service (TOS)
:P.The type of service for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MINDELAY, *MAXTHRPUT, *MAXRLB, *MINCOST.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPIFC/MTU'.Largest datagram (MTU) (MTU)
:P.The largest datagram, in bytes, the interface sends without breaking
it up.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 576 to 16388.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LIND.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPIFC/AUTOSTART'.Start with TCP/IP (AUTOSTART)
:P.Whether to start with TCP/IP.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPIFC/LCLIFC'.Associated local interface (LCLIFC)
:P.The associated local interface for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPIFC/ALIASNAME'.Alias name (ALIASNAME)
:P.The alias name for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 25 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPIFC/ADRPFXLEN'.Address prefix length (ADRPFXLEN)
:P.The prefix length of an IPv6 address&colon. how many leading bits
name the network.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 128.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 64 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPIFC/IFCID'.Interface identifier (IFCID)
:P.The interface identifier for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 16 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LIND.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPIFC/DADMAXTRN'.Duplicate address checks (DADMAXTRN)
:P.The duplicate address checks for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 10.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPIFC/PVYEXN'.Privacy extensions (PVYEXN)
:P.Whether to privacy extensions.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPIFC/PREFIFC'.Preferred interfaces (PREFIFC)
:P.The preferred interfaces for this command.
:P.Up to 10 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*AUTO:EPK.
:PD.Chosen automatically.
:PT.:PK.*DFTROUTE:EPK.
:PD.The default route, used when no other route matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPIFC/PREFLIND'.Preferred lines (PREFLIND)
:P.The preferred lines for this command.
:P.Up to 10 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Line description
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. VLAN identifier
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 4094.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPIFC/TEXT'.Text (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPIFC/DHCPDYNDNS'.DHCP dynamic DNS updates (DHCPDYNDNS)
:P.Whether to DHCP dynamic DNS updates.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPIFC/DHCPCLTID'.DHCP client identifier (DHCPCLTID)
:P.The DHCP client identifier for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ADPTADR, *DHCPUNQID.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPIFC/IP6GENGLBA'.Generate global addresses (IP6GENGLBA)
:P.Whether to generate global addresses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ADDTCPPORT.Add TCP/IP Port Restriction (ADDTCPPORT)
:P.Use the Add TCP/IP Port Restriction (ADDTCPPORT) command to keep a
port range for one user profile.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPPORT/PORT'.Port (PORT)
:P.The TCP or UDP port number.
:P.A value is required.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Lowest port
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Highest port
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPPORT/PROTOCOL'.Protocol (PROTOCOL)
:P.The protocol for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*UDP:EPK.
:PD.UDP.
:PT.:PK.*TCP:EPK.
:PD.TCP.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPPORT/USRPRF'.User profile allowed (USRPRF)
:P.The user profile the command uses.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ADDTCPRTE.Add TCP/IP Route (ADDTCPRTE)
:P.Use the Add TCP/IP Route (ADDTCPRTE) command to add a route to a
network or host.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPRTE/RTEDEST'.Destination (RTEDEST)
:P.The destination for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DFTROUTE:EPK.
:PD.The default route, used when no other route matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DFTMCAST, *DFT6ROUTE, *DFT6MCAST.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPRTE/SUBNETMASK'.Subnet mask (SUBNETMASK)
:P.The subnet mask that tells the network part of the address from the
host part.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*HOST:EPK.
:PD.A host route&colon. the address names a single host.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPRTE/TOS'.Type of service (TOS)
:P.The type of service for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MINDELAY, *MAXTHRPUT, *MAXRLB, *MINCOST.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPRTE/NEXTHOP'.Next hop (NEXTHOP)
:P.The next hop for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPRTE/ADRPFXLEN'.Address prefix length (ADRPFXLEN)
:P.The prefix length of an IPv6 address&colon. how many leading bits
name the network.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*HOST:EPK.
:PD.A host route&colon. the address names a single host.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 128.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 64 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPRTE/BINDIFC'.Bind to interface (BINDIFC)
:P.The bind to interface for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPRTE/BINDLIND'.Bind to line (BINDLIND)
:P.The bind to line for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Line description
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. VLAN identifier
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 4094.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPRTE/MTU'.Largest datagram (MTU) (MTU)
:P.The largest datagram, in bytes, the interface sends without breaking
it up.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 576 to 16388.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *IFC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPRTE/METRIC'.Route metric (METRIC)
:P.The route metric for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPRTE/REDST'.Redistribute the route (REDST)
:P.Whether to redistribute the route.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPRTE/DUPRTEPTY'.Priority among duplicates (DUPRTEPTY)
:P.The priority among duplicates for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MEDIUM:EPK.
:PD.Medium.
:PT.:PK.*HIGH:EPK.
:PD.High.
:PT.:PK.*LOW:EPK.
:PD.Low.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 10.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPRTE/TEXT'.Text (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ADDTCPSVR.Add TCP/IP Server (ADDTCPSVR)
:P.Use the Add TCP/IP Server (ADDTCPSVR) command to define a server
STRTCPSVR can start.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPSVR/SVRSPCVAL'.Server special value (SVRSPCVAL)
:P.The server special value for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPSVR/PGM'.Server program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPSVR/SVRNAME'.Server name (SVRNAME)
:P.The server name for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 30 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPSVR/SVRTYPE'.Server type (SVRTYPE)
:P.The server type for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 30 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPSVR/AUTOSTART'.Start with TCP/IP (AUTOSTART)
:P.Whether to start with TCP/IP.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTCPSVR/TEXT'.Text (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CFGTCP.Configure TCP/IP (CFGTCP)
:P.The Configure TCP/IP (CFGTCP) command works with the TCP/IP
configuration menu.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CFGTCPAPP.Configure TCP/IP Applications (CFGTCPAPP)
:P.The Configure TCP/IP Applications (CFGTCPAPP) command works with the
TCP/IP applications menu.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CFGTCPAPP/APP'.Application (APP)
:P.The application for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DDM:EPK.
:PD.DDM.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SELECT, *SNMP, *ROUTED, *ROUTING, *TFTP,
*BOOTP, *DHCP, *TELNET, *FTP, *SMTP, *LPD, *HTTP, *POP, *REXEC, *DNS,
*NTP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGQAPA.Change QAP Attributes (CHGQAPA)
:P.Use the Change QAP Attributes (CHGQAPA) command to change the
attributes of the QAP server, kept in the TCP/IP server table in QUSRSYS
and read when the server starts.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGQAPA/AUTOSTART'.Autostart server (AUTOSTART)
:P.The autostart server for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGQAPA/PORT'.Port (PORT)
:P.The TCP or UDP port number.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGQAPA/IDLETIMO'.Session idle timeout (IDLETIMO)
:P.The session idle timeout for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 60 to 86400.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGTCPA.Change TCP/IP Attributes (CHGTCPA)
:P.The Change TCP/IP Attributes (CHGTCPA) command works with the stack's
attributes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/TCPKEEPALV'.Keep-alive interval (minutes) (TCPKEEPALV)
:P.The keep-alive interval (minutes) for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 40320.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/TCPURGPTR'.Urgent pointer convention (TCPURGPTR)
:P.The urgent pointer convention for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *BSD, *RFC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/TCPRCVBUF'.Receive buffer (bytes) (TCPRCVBUF)
:P.The receive buffer (bytes) for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 512 to 8388608.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/TCPSNDBUF'.Send buffer (bytes) (TCPSNDBUF)
:P.The send buffer (bytes) for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 512 to 8388608.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/TCPR1CNT'.First retransmit threshold (TCPR1CNT)
:P.The first retransmit threshold for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 15.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/TCPR2CNT'.Last retransmit threshold (TCPR2CNT)
:P.The last retransmit threshold for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 2 to 16.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/TCPMINRTM'.Shortest retransmit (ms) (TCPMINRTM)
:P.The shortest retransmit (ms) for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 100 to 1000.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/TCPCLOTIMO'.Closed connection wait (s) (TCPCLOTIMO)
:P.The closed connection wait (s) for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 14400.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/TCPCNNMSG'.Messages for closed links (TCPCNNMSG)
:P.The messages for closed links for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *THRESHOLD.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/UDPCKS'.Check UDP checksums (UDPCKS)
:P.The check UDP checksums for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/IPPATHMTU'.Path MTU discovery (IPPATHMTU)
:P.The path MTU discovery for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Discover
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Rediscover every (minutes)
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 5 to 40320.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ONCE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/IPDTGFWD'.Forward datagrams (IPDTGFWD)
:P.The forward datagrams for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/IPSRCRTG'.Accept source routes (IPSRCRTG)
:P.The accept source routes for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/IPRSBTIMO'.Reassembly wait (seconds) (IPRSBTIMO)
:P.The reassembly wait (seconds) for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 5 to 120.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/IPTTL'.Datagram lifetime (hops) (IPTTL)
:P.The datagram lifetime (hops) for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/IPQOSENB'.Quality of service (IPQOSENB)
:P.The quality of service for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TOS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/IPQOSBCH'.QoS datagram batching (IPQOSBCH)
:P.The qoS datagram batching for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MINDELAY.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/IPQOSTMR'.QoS timer (ms) (IPQOSTMR)
:P.The qoS timer (ms) for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 5 to 5000.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/IPDEADGATE'.Gateway checks (IPDEADGATE)
:P.The gateway checks for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Check
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*LINE:EPK.
:PD.Line data.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Every (minutes)
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 60.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/ARPTIMO'.ARP entry lifetime (minutes) (ARPTIMO)
:P.The ARP entry lifetime (minutes) for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 1440.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/ECN'.Explicit congestion notice (ECN)
:P.The explicit congestion notice for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/NFC'.File cache for servers (NFC)
:P.The file cache for servers for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CLEAR.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Use the cache
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Keep files (seconds)
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Cache size (MB)
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/LOGPCLERR'.Log protocol errors (LOGPCLERR)
:P.The log protocol errors for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/DHCPUNQID'.DHCP unique identifier (DHCPUNQID)
:P.The DHCP unique identifier for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Action
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DUID.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Identifier
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 60 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PENDING.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/IP6ERRLMT'.ICMPv6 error burst (IP6ERRLMT)
:P.The ICMPv6 error burst for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/IP6ERRRATE'.ICMPv6 error rate (ms) (IP6ERRRATE)
:P.The ICMPv6 error rate (ms) for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/IP6HOPLMT'.IPv6 hop limit (IP6HOPLMT)
:P.The IPv6 hop limit for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/IP6DUPRTLS'.IPv6 duplicate route sharing (IP6DUPRTLS)
:P.The IPv6 duplicate route sharing for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RTR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/IP6TMPAVL'.Temporary address life (days) (IP6TMPAVL)
:P.The temporary address life (days) for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 6 digits, 1 of them after the decimal point.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/IP6TMPAPL'.Temporary address use (days) (IP6TMPAPL)
:P.The temporary address use (days) for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 6 digits, 1 of them after the decimal point.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPA/IP6TMPAXP'.Prefixes, no temp addresses (IP6TMPAXP)
:P.The prefixes, no temp addresses for this command.
:P.Up to 5 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Prefix
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Prefix length
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 64.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGTCPDMN.Change TCP/IP Domain (CHGTCPDMN)
:P.The Change TCP/IP Domain (CHGTCPDMN) command works with the local
names and the name servers.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPDMN/HOSTNAME'.Local host name (HOSTNAME)
:P.The local host name for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 63 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPDMN/DMNNAME'.Local domain name (DMNNAME)
:P.The local domain name for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPDMN/DMNSCHLIST'.Domains to search (DMNSCHLIST)
:P.The domains to search for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPDMN/HOSTSCHPTY'.Search the host table first (HOSTSCHPTY)
:P.The search the host table first for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LOCAL:EPK.
:PD.This system.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *REMOTE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPDMN/INTNETADR'.Name servers (INTNETADR)
:P.An internet address in dotted decimal form (IPv4) or in colon form
(IPv6).
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. First
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Second
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Third
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPDMN/PORT'.Name server port (PORT)
:P.The TCP or UDP port number.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPDMN/PROTOCOL'.Name server protocol (PROTOCOL)
:P.The name server protocol for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*UDP:EPK.
:PD.UDP.
:PT.:PK.*TCP:EPK.
:PD.TCP.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPDMN/INLDMNSVR'.First name server asked (INLDMNSVR)
:P.The first name server asked for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ROTATE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPDMN/DMNSVRRTY'.Name server retries (DMNSVRRTY)
:P.The name server retries for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Attempts
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Seconds between
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPDMN/DNSSEC'.Validate with DNSSEC (DNSSEC)
:P.The validate with DNSSEC for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGTCPHTE.Change TCP/IP Host Table Entry (CHGTCPHTE)
:P.Use the Change TCP/IP Host Table Entry (CHGTCPHTE) command to change
the names or text of an address.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPHTE/INTNETADR'.Internet address (INTNETADR)
:P.An internet address in dotted decimal form (IPv4) or in colon form
(IPv6).
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPHTE/HOSTNAME'.Host names (HOSTNAME)
:P.The host names for this command.
:P.Up to 65 values can be given.
:P.The value has 1 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Name
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPHTE/TEXT'.Text (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGTCPIFC.Change TCP/IP Interface (CHGTCPIFC)
:P.Use the Change TCP/IP Interface (CHGTCPIFC) command to change an
interface.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPIFC/INTNETADR'.Internet address (INTNETADR)
:P.An internet address in dotted decimal form (IPv4) or in colon form
(IPv6).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*IP4DHCP:EPK.
:PD.The address is assigned by DHCP.
:PT.:PK.*IP6SAC:EPK.
:PD.The address is configured by IPv6 stateless autoconfiguration.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPIFC/LIND'.Line (LIND)
:P.The line description.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LOOPBACK, *VIRTUALIP, *OPC.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Line description
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. VLAN identifier
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 4094.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPIFC/SUBNETMASK'.Subnet mask (SUBNETMASK)
:P.The subnet mask that tells the network part of the address from the
host part.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*HOST:EPK.
:PD.A host route&colon. the address names a single host.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPIFC/TOS'.Type of service (TOS)
:P.The type of service for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MINDELAY, *MAXTHRPUT, *MAXRLB, *MINCOST.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPIFC/MTU'.Largest datagram (MTU) (MTU)
:P.The largest datagram, in bytes, the interface sends without breaking
it up.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 576 to 16388.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LIND.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPIFC/AUTOSTART'.Start with TCP/IP (AUTOSTART)
:P.The start with TCP/IP for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPIFC/LCLIFC'.Associated local interface (LCLIFC)
:P.The associated local interface for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPIFC/ALIASNAME'.Alias name (ALIASNAME)
:P.The alias name for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 25 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPIFC/ADRPFXLEN'.Address prefix length (ADRPFXLEN)
:P.The prefix length of an IPv6 address&colon. how many leading bits
name the network.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 128.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPIFC/IFCID'.Interface identifier (IFCID)
:P.The interface identifier for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 16 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LIND.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPIFC/DADMAXTRN'.Duplicate address checks (DADMAXTRN)
:P.The duplicate address checks for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 10.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPIFC/PVYEXN'.Privacy extensions (PVYEXN)
:P.The privacy extensions for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPIFC/PREFIFC'.Preferred interfaces (PREFIFC)
:P.The preferred interfaces for this command.
:P.Up to 10 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*AUTO:EPK.
:PD.Chosen automatically.
:PT.:PK.*DFTROUTE:EPK.
:PD.The default route, used when no other route matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPIFC/PREFLIND'.Preferred lines (PREFLIND)
:P.The preferred lines for this command.
:P.Up to 10 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Line description
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. VLAN identifier
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 4094.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPIFC/TEXT'.Text (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPIFC/DHCPDYNDNS'.DHCP dynamic DNS updates (DHCPDYNDNS)
:P.The DHCP dynamic DNS updates for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPIFC/DHCPCLTID'.DHCP client identifier (DHCPCLTID)
:P.The DHCP client identifier for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ADPTADR, *DHCPUNQID.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPIFC/IP6GENGLBA'.Generate global addresses (IP6GENGLBA)
:P.The generate global addresses for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGTCPRTE.Change TCP/IP Route (CHGTCPRTE)
:P.Use the Change TCP/IP Route (CHGTCPRTE) command to change a route.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPRTE/RTEDEST'.Destination (RTEDEST)
:P.The destination for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DFTROUTE:EPK.
:PD.The default route, used when no other route matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DFTMCAST, *DFT6ROUTE, *DFT6MCAST.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPRTE/SUBNETMASK'.Subnet mask (SUBNETMASK)
:P.The subnet mask that tells the network part of the address from the
host part.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*HOST:EPK.
:PD.A host route&colon. the address names a single host.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPRTE/TOS'.Type of service (TOS)
:P.The type of service for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MINDELAY, *MAXTHRPUT, *MAXRLB, *MINCOST.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPRTE/NEXTHOP'.Next hop (NEXTHOP)
:P.The next hop for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPRTE/ADRPFXLEN'.Address prefix length (ADRPFXLEN)
:P.The prefix length of an IPv6 address&colon. how many leading bits
name the network.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*HOST:EPK.
:PD.A host route&colon. the address names a single host.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 128.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 64 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPRTE/BINDIFC'.Bind to interface (BINDIFC)
:P.The bind to interface for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPRTE/BINDLIND'.Bind to line (BINDLIND)
:P.The bind to line for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Line description
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. VLAN identifier
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 4094.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPRTE/MTU'.Largest datagram (MTU) (MTU)
:P.The largest datagram, in bytes, the interface sends without breaking
it up.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 576 to 16388.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *IFC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPRTE/METRIC'.Route metric (METRIC)
:P.The route metric for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPRTE/REDST'.Redistribute the route (REDST)
:P.The redistribute the route for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPRTE/DUPRTEPTY'.Priority among duplicates (DUPRTEPTY)
:P.The priority among duplicates for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*HIGH:EPK.
:PD.High.
:PT.:PK.*MEDIUM:EPK.
:PD.Medium.
:PT.:PK.*LOW:EPK.
:PD.Low.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 10.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPRTE/TEXT'.Text (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGTCPSVR.Change TCP/IP Server (CHGTCPSVR)
:P.Use the Change TCP/IP Server (CHGTCPSVR) command to change a
user-defined server.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPSVR/SVRSPCVAL'.Server special value (SVRSPCVAL)
:P.The server special value for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPSVR/PGM'.Server program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPSVR/SVRNAME'.Server name (SVRNAME)
:P.The server name for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 30 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPSVR/SVRTYPE'.Server type (SVRTYPE)
:P.The server type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 30 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPSVR/AUTOSTART'.Start with TCP/IP (AUTOSTART)
:P.The start with TCP/IP for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTCPSVR/TEXT'.Text (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CPYTCPHT.Copy TCP/IP Host Table (CPYTCPHT)
:P.Use the Copy TCP/IP Host Table (CPYTCPHT) command to copy the host
table to a file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTCPHT/TOFILE'.To file (TOFILE)
:P.The file that receives the data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QTCPHT is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTCPHT/TOMBR'.To member (TOMBR)
:P.The member of the to-file that receives the data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTCPHT/MBROPT'.Replace or add records (MBROPT)
:P.What happens to an existing member that receives data&colon. its
records are replaced, or the new records are added after them.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.What is there is replaced.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The new entries are added to what is there.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTCPHT/TOOBJ'.To stream file (TOOBJ)
:P.The to stream file for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTCPHT/REPLACE'.Replace the stream file (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDTCP.End TCP/IP (ENDTCP)
:P.Use the End TCP/IP (ENDTCP) command to end TCP/IP&colon. its servers,
then every interface.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDTCP/OPTION'.How to end (OPTION)
:P.The how to end for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:PT.:PK.*CNTRLD:EPK.
:PD.In a controlled way&colon. running work is given time to end on its
own.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDTCP/DELAY'.Delay for *CNTRLD (seconds) (DELAY)
:P.How many seconds a controlled end waits before the end becomes
immediate.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 86400.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 30 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDTCP/ENDSVR'.End the servers (ENDSVR)
:P.Whether to end the servers.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDTCPABN.End TCP/IP Abnormal (ENDTCPABN)
:P.Use the End TCP/IP Abnormal (ENDTCPABN) command to end TCP/IP at
once, without ending servers in order.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDTCPIFC.End TCP/IP Interface (ENDTCPIFC)
:P.Use the End TCP/IP Interface (ENDTCPIFC) command to end one
interface.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDTCPIFC/INTNETADR'.Internet address (INTNETADR)
:P.An internet address in dotted decimal form (IPv4) or in colon form
(IPv6).
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*IP4DHCP:EPK.
:PD.The address is assigned by DHCP.
:PT.:PK.*IP6SAC:EPK.
:PD.The address is configured by IPv6 stateless autoconfiguration.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=MRGTCPHT.Merge TCP/IP Host Table (MRGTCPHT)
:P.Use the Merge TCP/IP Host Table (MRGTCPHT) command to merge a host
file into the host table.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MRGTCPHT/FROMFILE'.From file (FROMFILE)
:P.The file the data comes from.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MRGTCPHT/FROMMBR'.From member (FROMMBR)
:P.The member the data comes from.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MRGTCPHT/FROMOBJ'.From stream file (FROMOBJ)
:P.The from stream file for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MRGTCPHT/FILEFMT'.File format (FILEFMT)
:P.The file format for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*AS400:EPK.
:PD.This system's native format.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OPSYS, *AIX, *NIC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MRGTCPHT/REPLACE'.Replace the table (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVNETTBLE.Remove Network Table Entry (RMVNETTBLE)
:P.Use the Remove Network Table Entry (RMVNETTBLE) command to remove a
network from the network table.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVNETTBLE/NETWORK'.Network (NETWORK)
:P.The network for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVPCLTBLE.Remove Protocol Table Entry (RMVPCLTBLE)
:P.Use the Remove Protocol Table Entry (RMVPCLTBLE) command to remove a
protocol from the protocol table.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVPCLTBLE/PROTOCOL'.Protocol (PROTOCOL)
:P.The protocol for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVSRVTBLE.Remove Service Table Entry (RMVSRVTBLE)
:P.Use the Remove Service Table Entry (RMVSRVTBLE) command to remove a
service from the services table.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVSRVTBLE/SERVICE'.Service (SERVICE)
:P.The service for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVSRVTBLE/PORT'.Port (PORT)
:P.The TCP or UDP port number.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVSRVTBLE/PROTOCOL'.Protocol (PROTOCOL)
:P.The protocol for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVTCPHTE.Remove TCP/IP Host Table Entry (RMVTCPHTE)
:P.Use the Remove TCP/IP Host Table Entry (RMVTCPHTE) command to remove
an address from the host table.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVTCPHTE/INTNETADR'.Internet address (INTNETADR)
:P.An internet address in dotted decimal form (IPv4) or in colon form
(IPv6).
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVTCPIFC.Remove TCP/IP Interface (RMVTCPIFC)
:P.Use the Remove TCP/IP Interface (RMVTCPIFC) command to remove an
interface.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVTCPIFC/INTNETADR'.Internet address (INTNETADR)
:P.An internet address in dotted decimal form (IPv4) or in colon form
(IPv6).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*IP4DHCP:EPK.
:PD.The address is assigned by DHCP.
:PT.:PK.*IP6SAC:EPK.
:PD.The address is configured by IPv6 stateless autoconfiguration.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVTCPIFC/ALIASNAME'.Alias name (ALIASNAME)
:P.The alias name for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 25 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVTCPIFC/LIND'.Line (LIND)
:P.The line description.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ADRALIAS.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Line description
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. VLAN identifier
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 4094.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVTCPPORT.Remove TCP/IP Port Restriction (RMVTCPPORT)
:P.Use the Remove TCP/IP Port Restriction (RMVTCPPORT) command to remove
port restrictions.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVTCPPORT/PORT'.Port (PORT)
:P.The TCP or UDP port number.
:P.A value is required.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Lowest port
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Highest port
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVTCPPORT/PROTOCOL'.Protocol (PROTOCOL)
:P.The protocol for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*UDP:EPK.
:PD.UDP.
:PT.:PK.*TCP:EPK.
:PD.TCP.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVTCPPORT/USRPRF'.User profile allowed (USRPRF)
:P.The user profile the command uses.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVTCPRTE.Remove TCP/IP Route (RMVTCPRTE)
:P.Use the Remove TCP/IP Route (RMVTCPRTE) command to remove a route.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVTCPRTE/RTEDEST'.Destination (RTEDEST)
:P.The destination for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DFTROUTE:EPK.
:PD.The default route, used when no other route matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DFTMCAST, *DFT6ROUTE, *DFT6MCAST.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVTCPRTE/SUBNETMASK'.Subnet mask (SUBNETMASK)
:P.The subnet mask that tells the network part of the address from the
host part.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*HOST:EPK.
:PD.A host route&colon. the address names a single host.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVTCPRTE/TOS'.Type of service (TOS)
:P.The type of service for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NORMAL:EPK.
:PD.Normal.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MINDELAY, *MAXTHRPUT, *MAXRLB, *MINCOST.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVTCPRTE/NEXTHOP'.Next hop (NEXTHOP)
:P.The next hop for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVTCPRTE/ADRPFXLEN'.Address prefix length (ADRPFXLEN)
:P.The prefix length of an IPv6 address&colon. how many leading bits
name the network.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*HOST:EPK.
:PD.A host route&colon. the address names a single host.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 128.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 64 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVTCPRTE/BINDIFC'.Bind to interface (BINDIFC)
:P.The bind to interface for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVTCPRTE/BINDLIND'.Bind to line (BINDLIND)
:P.The bind to line for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Line description
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. VLAN identifier
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 4094.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVTCPSVR.Remove TCP/IP Server (RMVTCPSVR)
:P.Use the Remove TCP/IP Server (RMVTCPSVR) command to remove a
user-defined server.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVTCPSVR/SVRSPCVAL'.Server special value (SVRSPCVAL)
:P.The server special value for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RNMTCPHTE.Rename TCP/IP Host Table Entry (RNMTCPHTE)
:P.Use the Rename TCP/IP Host Table Entry (RNMTCPHTE) command to move a
host table entry to a new address.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RNMTCPHTE/INTNETADR'.Internet address (INTNETADR)
:P.An internet address in dotted decimal form (IPv4) or in colon form
(IPv6).
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RNMTCPHTE/NEWINTNETA'.New internet address (NEWINTNETA)
:P.The new internet address for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STRTCP.Start TCP/IP (STRTCP)
:P.Use the Start TCP/IP (STRTCP) command to start TCP/IP&colon. the
interfaces, routes and servers that start with it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTCP/STRSVR'.Start the servers (STRSVR)
:P.Whether to start the servers.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTCP/STRIFC'.Start the interfaces (STRIFC)
:P.Whether to start the interfaces.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTCP/STRPTPPRF'.Start point-to-point profiles (STRPTPPRF)
:P.Whether to start point-to-point profiles.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTCP/STRIP6'.Start IPv6 (STRIP6)
:P.Whether to start IPv6.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STRTCPIFC.Start TCP/IP Interface (STRTCPIFC)
:P.Use the Start TCP/IP Interface (STRTCPIFC) command to start one
interface, or every autostart one.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRTCPIFC/INTNETADR'.Internet address (INTNETADR)
:P.An internet address in dotted decimal form (IPv4) or in colon form
(IPv6).
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*IP4DHCP:EPK.
:PD.The address is assigned by DHCP.
:PT.:PK.*IP6SAC:EPK.
:PD.The address is configured by IPv6 stateless autoconfiguration.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 45 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *AUTOSTART.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKNETTBLE.Work with Network Table Entries (WRKNETTBLE)
:P.Use the Work with Network Table Entries (WRKNETTBLE) command to work
with the network table.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKPCLTBLE.Work with Protocol Table Entries (WRKPCLTBLE)
:P.Use the Work with Protocol Table Entries (WRKPCLTBLE) command to work
with the protocol table.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKSRVTBLE.Work with Service Table Entries (WRKSRVTBLE)
:P.Use the Work with Service Table Entries (WRKSRVTBLE) command to work
with the services table.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
